id: hac-ln1v
title: Add agent-native media discovery and search
description: "Expose current Home Assistant media source and media player browse, search, and resolve WebSocket contracts through a typed, bounded, read-only CLI surface."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 0
tags[6]: agents,api,home-assistant,media,search,websocket
created_at: "2026-07-25T22:30:56.902Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-25T22:30:56.902Z"
deadline: "2026-07-27T22:30:56.902Z"
assignee: unbraind
author: codex-root
estimated_minutes: 360
acceptance_criteria: "hassio media browse, search, and resolve expose the official WebSocket payloads with detailed recursive help and pre-network validation; Search supports media-player and media-source scopes, current media-class filters, count and positive bounded limits, stable machine-readable output, and honest unsupported-command errors; Built and installed hassio passes formatter, schema, help, isolated wizard, live read-only, package, security, release-dry-run, and PM acceptance; All source coverage and docstrings remain 100 percent, source files remain at or below 300 code lines, and no private live details enter Git or PM"
definition_of_ready: "Official docs, Core dev source, installed dependency contracts, all-status PM lineage, current GitHub state, and redacted live capability probes have been inspected"
goal: complete-home-assistant-api-coverage
objective: agent-native-media-discovery
value: Agents can discover playable media and search supported providers without hand-authoring opaque WebSocket payloads.
impact: Adds token-bounded read-only discovery for one of Home Assistant 2026.7 development cycle most relevant API additions.
outcome: A stable typed CLI contract that works on supported servers and fails transparently on older capability sets.
why_now: "Home Assistant added searchable media sources in July 2026, while this CLI only offers generic WebSocket passthrough."
parent: hac-4s9j
reviewer: unbraind
risk: high
confidence: 96
sprint: 2026-07-media-discovery
release: 2026.7.26
