comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-25T22:30:56.902Z",codex-root,All-status keyword searches found no canonical media discovery or search delivery item; this feature extends rather than duplicates the closed general API parity lineage.
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-25T22:30:56.902Z",codex-root,"Never persist raw browse trees, search results, media identifiers, signed URLs, entity IDs, or local instance details. Durable evidence is limited to versions, command names, counts, booleans, and exit classifications."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-25T22:30:56.902Z",codex-root,"Current Core dev defines media_source/search_media with media_content_id, search_query, and optional media_filter_classes; local stable 2026.7.4 does not yet register that newest command."
files[1]{path,scope,note}:
  src/commands/media.ts,project,existing media command boundary
tests[1]{command,scope,timeout_seconds,pm_context_mode}:
  "bun run release:verify",project,2400,tracker
docs[1]{path,scope,note}:
  docs/API.md,project,canonical command reference
body: "Official Home Assistant 2026.7-era documentation and current Core dev source add searchable media sources while retaining media player search, browse, and resolve contracts. The local Core 2026.7.4 supports media player search and media source browse, but correctly reports the newer media source search command as unavailable. Deliver a typed surface that validates current media classes, bounds agent output, preserves generic passthrough, and reports server capability failures without masking them."
